# Cloudflare Pages headers file.
#
# Purpose: keep the DEV preview site (dev.bendentremont.com, served by Cloudflare
# Pages from the `dev` branch) out of search engines, so it can never outrank or
# duplicate the real production site (bendentremont.com, served by GitHub Pages
# from `main`).
#
# X-Robots-Tag: noindex is the strongest de-index signal — Google honors it fully.
#
# MERGE-SAFE: this file only affects Cloudflare Pages. GitHub Pages (which serves
# production from `main`) does NOT process `_headers`, and because it runs Jekyll
# with no `.nojekyll`, it excludes underscore-prefixed files from the build
# entirely. So even when `dev` merges into `main`, production indexing is unaffected.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# NOTE: Cloudflare Pages caches CSS/JS for 4h and ignores Cache-Control set here
# (it enforces its own asset caching). To force fresh CSS/JS we cache-bust via a
# ?v=<version> query on the <link>/<script> tags in index.html — bump it whenever
# styles.css or script.js changes.
